From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:18:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] Find the caller's stack pointer without an MSVC
 intrinsic

mingw-w64 declares _AddressOfReturnAddress() but nothing defines it.

Upstream: not submitted; part of the Windows/gcc port, not upstream OpenJDK
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hotspot/os_cpu/windows_x86/os_windows_x86.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/hotspot/os_cpu/windows_x86/os_windows_x86.cpp b/src/hotspot/os_cpu/windows_x86/os_windows_x86.cpp
index 8e934bc48..01d8340a1 100644
--- a/src/hotspot/os_cpu/windows_x86/os_windows_x86.cpp
+++ b/src/hotspot/os_cpu/windows_x86/os_windows_x86.cpp
@@ -253,9 +253,15 @@ intptr_t* os::fetch_bcp_from_context(const void* ucVoid) {
 // saved by that call instruction. Therefore, the stack pointer of the caller
 // just before the call instruction, is acquired by skipping over the return PC
 // slot in the stack.
-__declspec(noinline)
+NOINLINE
 address os::current_stack_pointer() {
+#ifdef __GNUC__
+  // gcc lacks _AddressOfReturnAddress(); with frame pointers the return PC
+  // slot sits right above the saved frame pointer.
+  return ((address)__builtin_frame_address(0)) + 2 * sizeof(void*);
+#else
   return ((address)_AddressOfReturnAddress()) + sizeof(void*);
+#endif
 }
 
 bool os::win32::get_frame_at_stack_banging_point(JavaThread* thread,
